# 🎯 0. Executive Summary
We are going to add **LIVE** mode to Cerberus-V (as opposed to *SIMULATION*).  
The switch must be **latent-safe** — i.e. even if the operator accidentally enables it at 03:00 Moscow time, the worst outcome is *rate-limited discard*, not *total blackout*.

---

# ⚠️ 1. Threat Model for LIVE Mode

| Failure Vector | Worst Case | Mitigation Implemented |
|---|---|---|
| **Rule race** | Drop legitimate 0-RTT TLS → broken API | Two-phase commit + shadow map |
| **Map exhaustion** | ENOSPC → panic | per-CPU LRU + atomic swap |
| **NIC reset** | XDP detach → 100 % loss | watchdog + auto-re-attach |
| **VPP crash** | 100 Gbps → 0 Gbps | systemd-restart + BPF fallback |
| **Human error** | “block 0.0.0.0/0” | protected *immutable* baseline rule |
| **Memory leak** | OOM → host freeze | cgroup memory.max + PSI oomd |

